image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_012_thumb.jpg", "page": "12", "label": "12", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/12"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_013_thumb.jpg", "page": "13", "label": "13", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/13"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_014_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "14", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/14"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_015_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "15", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/15"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_016_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "16", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/16"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_017_thumb.jpg", "page": "17", "label": "17", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/17"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_017-01_thumb.jpg", "page": "18", "label": "[18]", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/18"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD6", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "editorialPageNumber": "16", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/21225849/21225849-0016.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> down from their spiritual wickednes in high places and from their strong holds of the divine a flud of dirt and mire and filthiness and vomit upon our heads no God forbid. hell may poor forth its rage like the burning lavy [lava] of mount vesuvias or of Etna or of the most terible of the burning mountains and yet shall mormonism stand. watter, fire, truth, and god are all the same truth is mormonism God is the author of it he is our shield<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12668345360737541342\"><a href=\"#12668345360737541342\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans76\"><span id=\"documenttrans76\">76</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 2 Samuel 22:3; Psalm 84:9; and Proverbs 30:5.</p><hr></div></div></aside> it is by him we received our birth, it was by his voice that we were called to a <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15513717260023432032\"><a href=\"#15513717260023432032\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4078\" topic=\"x4078\" title=\"Dispensation\">dispensation</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Dispensation\"><p>A gift of divine knowledge, power, and authority from God to humankind; often associated with a prophet and his time period. A revelation published in 1835 identified JS and Oliver Cowdery as the recipients of keys to administer a final dispensation of the...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/dispensation\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> of his gospel in the begining of the fullness of times it was by him we received the <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830\" class=\"reference\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/book-of-mormon-1830\" poptitle=\"Book of Mormon, 1830\">book of mormon</a> and it was by him that we remain unto this day and by him we shall remain if it shall be for our glory and in his almighty name we are determined to indure tribulation<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16856488185525487663\"><a href=\"#16856488185525487663\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans77\"><span id=\"documenttrans77\">77</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 2 Thessalonians 1:4.</p><hr></div></div></aside> as good soldiers unto the end but brethren we shall continue to offer further reflections in our next <a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839\" class=\"reference\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839\" poptitle=\"Letter to Edward Partridge and the Church, circa 22 March 1839\">epistle</a> you will learn by the time you have read this and if you do not learn it you may learn it that walls and iron doors and screaking hinges and half scard to death Guards and jailors grining like some damned spirit lest an inocent man should make his escape to bring to light the damnible deeds of a murderous mob is calculated in its verry nature to make the sole of an honist man feel stronger than the powers of hell. But we must bring our epistle to a close [p. 16]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> down from their spiritual wickednes in hig[h] <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>places and from their strong holds of the divin[e] <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>a flud of dirt and mire and filthiness and <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>vomit upon our heads no God forbid. hell may <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>poor forth its rage like the burning lavy [lava] of <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>mount vesuvias or of Etna or of the most <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>terible of the burning mountains and yet <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>shall mormonism stand. watter, fire, truth, and <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>god are all the same truth is mormonism God is the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>author of it he is our shield<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7474005687677318145\"><a href=\"#7474005687677318145\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans76\"><span id=\"documenttrans76\">76</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 2 Samuel 22:3; Psalm 84:9; and Proverbs 30:5.</p><hr></div></div></aside> it is by him we received <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>our birth, it was by his voice that we were called <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>to <span class=\"deleted\">in</span> a <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2747879743668715454\"><a href=\"#2747879743668715454\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4078\" topic=\"x4078\" title=\"Dispensation\">dispensation</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Dispensation\"><p>A gift of divine knowledge, power, and authority from God to humankind; often associated with a prophet and his time period. A revelation published in 1835 identified JS and Oliver Cowdery as the recipients of keys to administer a final dispensation of the...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/dispensation\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> of his gospel in the begining of <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the fullness of tim[e]s it was by him we received the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830\" class=\"reference\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/book-of-mormon-1830\" poptitle=\"Book of Mormon, 1830\">book of mormon</a> and it was by him that we <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>remain unto this day and by him we shall remain <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>if it shall be for our glory and in his almighty <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>name we are determined to indure tribulation<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17780307925392773237\"><a href=\"#17780307925392773237\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans77\"><span id=\"documenttrans77\">77</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 2 Thessalonians 1:4.</p><hr></div></div></aside> as <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>good soldiers unto the end but brethren we shall <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>continue to offer further reflections in our next <a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839\" class=\"reference\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839\" poptitle=\"Letter to Edward Partridge and the Church, circa 22 March 1839\"><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>epistle</a> you will learn by the time you have read <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>this and if you do not learn it you may learn it <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>that walls and &lt;​iron​&gt; doors &lt;​and screaking hinges​&gt; <span class=\"deleted\">is only calcu</span> and half scard to <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>death Guards and jailors grining like some damn<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>ed spirit lest an inocent man should make his esc<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>ape to bring to light the damnible deeds of a murderous <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>mob is cal[c]ulated in its verry nature to make the sole <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>of an honist man feel stronger than the powers <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>of hell. But we must bring our epistle to a close [p. 16]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/1", "versionFeatured": "true"}, {"versionTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839, as Published in <em xmlns:tei=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" xmlns:lds=\"https://ldsc.xmlref.com/local/ldschurch\">Times and Seasons</em>", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839-as-published-in-times-and-seasons/1", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": " History, 1838–1856, volume C-1 [2 November 1838–31 July 1842]", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-1838-1856-volume-c-1-2-november-1838-31-july-1842/81", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "“History of Joseph Smith”", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-of-joseph-smith/333", "versionFeatured": ""}], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_016_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_016_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_016.jpg", "downloadImageUrl": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_016_download.jpg"}, "imageCredit": "", "facsimile": "", "dzUrlXml": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_016.xml", "classification": "Documents", "publishedStatus": "FinalContent", "accessionNumber": "430", "requestedPageNumber": "16", "numberOfPages": "18", "editorialTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "cleanEditorialTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "date": "March 20, 1839", "handwriting": "Handwriting of Alexander McRae and Caleb Baldwin, with insertions by JS", "footnotes": [{"